<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Conasupo to supply 1.9 mln T corn in '97.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Conasupo to supply 1.9 mln T corn in '97.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's national staples agency Conasupo will supply 1.9 million tonnes of corn to the tortilla industry this year, the government agency said in a statement obtained Monday.</p>
<p>In the current crop campaign which started in October, Conasupo said it has bought more than 1.5 million tonnes of white corn to date</p>
<p>Conasupo is the agency through which the government offers a floor price to Mexican corn farmers, and then resells the grain to corn flour and tortilla industrialists at subsidised prices for the production of corn pancake tortillas.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
